# Stage 20.3 — dedicated test database. Loaded ONLY by vitest.setup.ts (with
# `override: true`, on top of `.env`) when NODE_ENV=test, which Vitest sets
# automatically. This MUST point at a database that is separate from your
# `.env`'s DATABASE_URL — never reuse your development database for tests.
#
# `assertTestDatabaseSafety()` (src/server/testing/db-safety.ts) refuses to
# run any DB-backed test unless the connected database is EXACTLY
# `trading_hub_test` — so even if this file is missing or misconfigured,
# tests fail loudly instead of silently touching your development data.
#
# First-time setup: copy this file to `.env.test`, then run
# `npm run test:db:setup` to create `trading_hub_test` and apply migrations.
DATABASE_URL="postgresql://trading_hub:trading_hub_dev@localhost:5432/trading_hub_test?schema=public"
